## Why This Is Asked

Tests a candidate's ability to design an end-to-end, event-driven ingestion with privacy controls, multi-tenant isolation, and idempotent writes in a beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts

- Cloud Functions triggers on Cloud Storage object finalize
- Schema validation and per-tenant data routing
- PII redaction driven by a policies.json file
- BigQuery partitioning by tenant and date
- Idempotent writes using insertId
- Minimal IAM bindings and simple error handling

## Code Example

```javascript
// skeleton: Cloud Function triggered on new object
exports.handleFile = async (data, context) => {
  // 1) read file from data.name in data.bucket
  // 2) parse JSON, validate required fields
  // 3) redact according to policies.json
  // 4) write to BigQuery with insertId = tenant|event_id|ts
  // 5) publish to DLQ on error
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test redaction policy updates without reprocessing data?
- How handle mixed valid/invalid records within a single file and ensure idempotency?

